><ref id="ref36"><label>36</label><citation citation-type="journal">Bai, T., Becker, M., Gupta, A., Strike, P., Murphy, V. J., Anders, R. F., and Batchelor, A. H. (<year>2005</year>) <source>Proc. Natl. Acad. Sci. U. S. A.</source> <volume>102</volume> <fpage>12736</fpage>&#x02013;12741<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16129835</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="N0x49e2db0N0x5c915c0"><label>37</label><citation citation-type="journal">Chen, B., Vogan, E. M., Gong, H., Skehel, J. J., Wiley, D. C., and Harrison, S. C. (<year>2005</year>) <source>Nature</source> <volume>433</volume> <fpage>834</fpage>&#x02013;841<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15729334</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ref38"><label>38</label><citation citation-type="journal">Skehel, J. J., and Wiley, D. C. (<year>2000</year>) <source>Annu. Rev. Biochem.</source> <volume>69</volume> <fpage>531</fpage>&#x02013;569<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10966468</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list><fn-group><fn id="fn3"><label>2</label><p>The abbreviations used are: PfEMP1, plasmodium falciparum erythrocyte membrane protein 1; DBL domain, Duffy binding-like domain; CSA, chondroitin sulfate A; PEG, polyethylene glycol; MES, 4-morpholineethanesulfonic acid.</p></fn></fn-group></back></article>